# Copy to apps/web/.env and fill in. .env is git-ignored; nothing in this file is a secret.
#
# Map tiles. There is no key any more and nothing to fill in here: the map is MapLibre drawing from
# an openly licensed endpoint that wants no account, and the endpoint, its licence, its attribution
# and its usage policy are packages/catalog/geography.json rather than an environment variable.
#
# Streets are off until the person looking asks for them, on every screen that draws a map. That is
# a privacy decision rather than a performance one: a tile request tells its server which square of
# the city is on screen, the internet address that asked and the time, and a default nobody chose is
# not agreement to disclose it. It is also what keeps the 1.8 MB map library out of a handset that
# never opens a map. The schematic — the same zones, visits and nurses, in their real positions,
# from the same contract, with no network call at all — is what draws until then, and it is a
# complete answer rather than a placeholder.
#
# Set this to off to build with no tile source at all. The switch then does not appear and the
# schematic is the whole map: the state both native apps are permanently in, and what a deployment
# behind a firewall that blocks the endpoint should ship rather than a switch that cannot work.
# Anything else, including leaving it unset, offers the switch.
#
# The tile server is asked for streets by tile coordinate and is told nothing about the caseload: no
# visit, no patient and no nurse position is ever sent to a mapping provider.
VITE_MAP_TILES=""
